# Copy this file to client/.env for local development.
# .env is gitignored — the real file is never committed.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, and it
# inlines them at BUILD time, not run time. Restart `npm run dev` after
# changing this file or the change won't be picked up.

# Your Web3Forms access key — get one free at https://web3forms.com
# (enter the inbox that should receive enquiries; the key is emailed to you).
#
# This value ends up visible in the built JavaScript. That's expected and
# safe: the key is write-only, it can only submit to your own form. It lives
# in an env var so it isn't committed to git, not because it's a secret.
#
# For the GitHub Pages build, set the SAME value as a repository secret
# named VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions).
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
